what's up guys i'm dave klein aka dave  control and i was fortunate enough to  get a hands-on experience with eldon  ring i was able to play the first  roughly seven hours of the game and even  went beyond where the network test ended  so i wanted to make a video about 12  interesting things i learned i think  it's going to go without saying that  there will be slight spoilers but like  you i know there are things i would hate  if they were spoiled for me so i'm going  to do my best to avoid anything like  that  bandai namco has been slowly revealing  the starting classes of alden ring the  current ones available as of my time  with the game were vagabond warrior hero  bandit astrologer prophet samurai  prisoner confessor and wretch with  wretch being the level 1 build  but just like any prior souls born game  your starting class is just that if you  don't like your stats every level up is  a chance to build your character in  another direction like adding more  strength to go full on strength build or  adding various magic stats if you want  to use some spells  every souls born game has had a rest  area where npcs gather and you can feel  a little bit of safety the roundtable  hold is eldon ring's version of this and  it isn't immediately available to the  player but once you do gain access to it  similar to the hub of other games npcs  will wander in and out of the area with  certain parts of the round table hold  being closed off until an event opens up  more places you can access  as far as i can tell this hub is  completely unreachable without warping  but who knows if that will change  through the network test we discovered  that estus flasks worked similarly to  dark souls 3. you'll have an hp recovery  estus flask and an fp recovery estus  flask with fp being focus points or the  way you can utilize magic and weapon  arts again like dark souls 3 you'll have  a total number of estes uses that you  can delegate between the two however you  like and in whatever way is best for  your build you'll also be able to  upgrade your estus flasks which will be  extremely useful as you reach more  challenging areas the way to do this is  with various seeds you'll find  throughout the game  golden seas are your way to upgrade the  number of flask uses you have and you  can find golden seeds a number of  different ways while you're probably  familiar with the massive herb trees  from the elton ring trailer there are  various sized herd trees with tiny ones  having golden seeds underneath them when  you first find them additionally there  are other ways to get your hands on  golden seeds including npc quest lines  as you level up your estus flask you'll  slowly need a larger number of golden  seeds for later upgrades in order to  upgrade the strength of your estus flask  and just how much it heals you you'll  need another kind of seed these seeds  can be found at various churches if  you've seen footage of the network test  you'll know about the church of dragon  communion players we're able to find  there are many other kinds of churches  and this is where i was able to find  this kind of seed in my experience  that said there may be other places to  find them this is just what i was able  to find in my short playthrough  one of the critiques of eldon ring has  been the game's spirit ashes there are  various spirit allies you can summon to  aid you in battle the critique mainly  comes from the network test and feeling  like these spirits were too powerful  however in the build i played there were  a number of ways their power was offset  we learned from the network test that  for one you can only summon these  spirits in special marked areas and they  aren't available anytime you want for  example i don't believe i was able to  summon them in the game's ever jails  additionally and this is probably the  most important point the spirits start  off relatively weak they'll also cost a  different amount of fp to summon and i  found a higher powered spirit that i  didn't have enough fp to summon in my  time playing the game  you can however level up your spirit  ashes similar to how you would upgrade a  weapon  in order to do so you'll need to find a  spirit tuner who will take grave glove  words you can find that as you'd imagine  work just like a blacksmith upgrading  your weapons with smithing stones  while i didn't specifically find ways to  upgrade armor in my short time playing  there was a sewing kit i found in the  game which allows you to customize your  armor it was hard for me to tell if this  was purely cosmetic or if there were  genuine stat differences but it's  something to keep in mind and keep an  eye out for i also found a painting that  you could not only look at but collect i  have no idea what the purpose is or if  it's going to be something like what  we've seen from dark souls 1 or 3 but  it's definitely an interesting new  feature  eldon ring definitely still has items  that are related to pvp i found a couple  mirrors which let you alter your  appearance in minor ways in order to  trick invaders into attempting to kill  the wrong player  one of my personal concerns in playing  the other ring network test was that  outside of the legacy dungeons all of  the other dungeons felt pretty barren  and small they felt a little more like  mini chalice dungeons than other areas  we've come to known from software games  that said in playing the full build of  the game i stumbled upon a far larger  dungeon that wasn't considered a legacy  dungeon it helps show that there will be  a wide variety of dungeon sizes you'll  find in eldon ring from larger to medium  sized and absolutely tiny mini dungeons  additionally all of these dungeons had  unique bosses with interesting loot to  find so from software is definitely  making exploration a worthwhile venture  in eldon ring  and speaking of dungeons let's talk  about legacy dungeons i had the  opportunity to play through stormville  and while i'm absolutely certain i  didn't see all of it i was able to make  it through godric and get a good feel of  the overall area stormville is massive  in scope and has plenty of different  wraparounds and interesting areas to  explore as you're not allowed to use  torrent your spectral steed and dungeons  it truly felt like a classic from  software experience if i were to compare  it to anything think of it like demon  souls imagine that you have boletaria  latria and the rest of the areas all  available in the game however instead of  needing to return to a hub to access  these areas the full map of the realm is  yours to explore and you'll stumble  across boletaria you'll stumble across  latria size and scope-wise is hard to  tell just how large all of the legacy  dungeons will be so i honestly can't  tell you if the aries will be more akin  to the cathedral of the deep or irithyll  the boreal valley in size or something  as large as scale as boletaria or latria  going back to dark souls 2 there were  unique items in that game called  ferris's lockstones these lockstones  unlocked special areas that had special  goodies hidden away they were one time  use so it was up to you to find more of  these lockstones so you could unlock  every hidden area  alden ring has an item that works in the  exact same way called a stone sword key  there's plenty of variety in what's  behind these keys including locked away  ever jails areas with hidden treasures  and even dungeons  something interesting and brand new to  eldon ring was the way in which you seem  to unlock the game's accessories or  charms while you start the game with one  of these slots after defeating a certain  boss just by defeating that boss i  automatically unlocked one of these  slots i can't say for certain how many  slots you'll gain or if this is how  every slot will be unlocked but it's  definitely an interesting change that's  worth noting  the lore of the game that has been  revealed to us has made it clear how  important great runes are to the story  in fact the way you level up in the game  is by finding basic runes they act like  your souls or blood echoes from souls  born games in being both your form of  currency and way to level up  like those games you'll gain them for  defeating enemies or finding special  items that will give you rooms for using  them  great runes on the other hand are unique  equippable items you'll be able to find  that grant you specific blessings and  abilities i don't want to ruin which i  found or what it did but it's an  interesting thing to note  once you make it outside the tutorial  area and into limgrave the world truly  is your oyster there are definitely  smarter and easier paths the game pushes  you into taking  but you can seemingly go wherever you  want right away it's a refreshing and  different experience and as exploration  seems to be well handled in eldon ring  it's certainly shaping up to be a game  that will be incredible to explore  and there you have 12 things i learned  playing elton ring i hope you learned  something that interested you and i  answered some questions you might have  february 25th cannot come soon enough  and i can't wait to see all you lowly  tarnish soon  [Music]  you
 

